    {
      "caption": "Mitochondria: folded cristae, huge surface area",
      "duration_ms": 10000,
      "id": "s1",
      "narration": "The mitochondrion is the site of aerobic respiration. Its inner membrane folds into shelves called cristae. The folding packs an enormous surface area into a tiny space — room for the machinery that makes ATP.",
