    {
      "caption": "Photosynthesis: photolysis and the Calvin cycle",
      "duration_ms": 11000,
      "id": "s5",
      "narration": "In the light-dependent stage, water is split — photolysis — releasing oxygen and the hydrogen needed for the next stage. Then the Calvin cycle, needing no light directly, fixes carbon dioxide into carbohydrate in the stroma.",
