    {
      "caption": "Limiting factors — and a misconception",
      "duration_ms": 10000,
      "id": "s6",
      "narration": "The rate of photosynthesis is capped by whichever factor is in shortest supply — light intensity, carbon dioxide concentration, or temperature. And one correction: plants do not only respire at night. They respire around the clock; at night there is simply no photosynthesis to hide it.",
